                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5af9adae-5a12-3bad-b771-2acfc5fcfb99",
                        "entry_id": "700b7626-94ba-36cb-820b-25b2613378fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "drückt aus, dass etwas auf jeden Fall und unabhängig von allem eintritt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aae784c7-5089-4cf0-a28b-e80ec9159099",
                                "sense_id": "5af9adae-5a12-3bad-b771-2acfc5fcfb99",
                                "text": "Mich interessiert ohnedies, woher all diese Schaben in der Küche kommen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5757ca8-1eed-40cd-b3b6-bfbff113c264",
                                "sense_id": "5af9adae-5a12-3bad-b771-2acfc5fcfb99",
                                "text": "Forcher selbst meint dazu, man würde im Fernsehen ohnedies zu viel Hässliches sehen, er möchte die schönen Seiten zeigen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "614df54d-4905-4b37-bcd8-02acdb1a1e8d",
                        "source_entry_id": "700b7626-94ba-36cb-820b-25b2613378fc",
                        "source_sense_id": "5af9adae-5a12-3bad-b771-2acfc5fcfb99",
                        "source_sense_description": "drückt aus, dass etwas auf jeden Fall und unabhängig von allem eintritt",
                        "target_lang_word": "in any case",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "in any case",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "453cbeb0-1473-3adc-950c-d17ded0cea67",
                                        "entry_id": "af849dda-7a81-3b95-88c5-b02b328fd489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Whatever be the case."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5af30d00-9865-4f22-a5c9-844c150ca21b",
                                                "sense_id": "453cbeb0-1473-3adc-950c-d17ded0cea67",
                                                "text": "Who knows how many more inches of snow will fall tonight, but in any case, we can expect to be doing a lot of shoveling tomorrow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f040ec8d-3f13-4b49-94d7-ebf0a2060053",
                                                "sense_id": "453cbeb0-1473-3adc-950c-d17ded0cea67",
                                                "text": "Later Martin said, \"If we ever have another baby girl, I'm going to give her a simple name like Mary Jane.\" When we did have another daughter, we called her Bernice Albertine, after her two grandmothers. Not quite Mary Jane, but at least named for members of the family. In any case, she is known as Bunny,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c48be66b-bd0d-416f-ac2f-17c35390cfd1",
                                                "sense_id": "453cbeb0-1473-3adc-950c-d17ded0cea67",
                                                "text": "The Information Department is outhoused but there are operational reasons for this and it would, in any case, be physically impossible to house the staff of the Department in the main building."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31550733-bd5e-4d79-878e-5ee97603a773",
                                                "sense_id": "453cbeb0-1473-3adc-950c-d17ded0cea67",
                                                "text": "Because of the juristic difficulties associated with the Donation of Constantine, the question of whether the papacy had in any case prescribed its jurisdiction in the patrimony had become a common topic amongst jurists […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ffe5d7a-0214-39b4-8ce1-a67def60f157",
                                        "entry_id": "af849dda-7a81-3b95-88c5-b02b328fd489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see in, any, case."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e44218ce-c91c-4eff-8492-ecca98ed7e40",
                                                "sense_id": "9ffe5d7a-0214-39b4-8ce1-a67def60f157",
                                                "text": "Their most popular product, an assortment of ales, is packaged such that there are always at least two bottles of India pale ale in any case."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "73f0a0d5-bf65-4dea-bef5-dda2589e426b",
                        "source_entry_id": "700b7626-94ba-36cb-820b-25b2613378fc",
                        "source_sense_id": "5af9adae-5a12-3bad-b771-2acfc5fcfb99",
                        "source_sense_description": "drückt aus, dass etwas auf jeden Fall und unabhängig von allem eintritt",
                        "target_lang_word": "anyhow",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anyhow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "516bb592-5a7f-3ac5-8ce9-7913813a4967",
                                        "entry_id": "b59486c2-62d5-39ec-a382-2a408194a083",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In any way or manner whatever."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "83f427f9-5ba3-31f0-85dd-8e6488553f3b",
                                        "entry_id": "b59486c2-62d5-39ec-a382-2a408194a083",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In any case. Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "847d6881-4be4-4052-bf5a-e9038f139002",
                                                "sense_id": "83f427f9-5ba3-31f0-85dd-8e6488553f3b",
                                                "text": "Anyhow, he is dead now."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b977d98b-e64d-401e-a33c-5b0317efedcf",
                                                "sense_id": "83f427f9-5ba3-31f0-85dd-8e6488553f3b",
                                                "text": "I think they’re asleep; anyhow, they’re quiet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0940a240-1ee8-31f5-98f9-732c20d2e030",
                                        "entry_id": "b59486c2-62d5-39ec-a382-2a408194a083",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without care or tidiness; recklessly, negligently or randomly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "087e4759-0431-4e12-879f-0c1e72e37d94",
                                                "sense_id": "0940a240-1ee8-31f5-98f9-732c20d2e030",
                                                "text": "It was a woman’s clothing, beyond a doubt, all thrown in anyhow, — as if the person who had placed it there had been in a desperate hurry."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6f9d7d0-facd-353b-92c4-b6069ec9f54d",
                                        "entry_id": "b59486c2-62d5-39ec-a382-2a408194a083",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Thoughtlessly, randomly, without careful consideration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Singapore",
                                            "Singlish",
                                            "broadly",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "anyhow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b4fe65b5-8313-3cdb-b4b8-853a0ebd9049",
                                        "entry_id": "5f7b4bb6-2c74-3b52-8b75-e06f6d4d5659",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Random, careless, offhand, disorderly; done without thought or consideration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Singapore",
                                            "Singlish",
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "predicative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a61365b-129d-46bb-be37-36d8ae9f8052",
                                                "sense_id": "b4fe65b5-8313-3cdb-b4b8-853a0ebd9049",
                                                "text": "Rabak, to refer to something messed up: Eh bro, your hairdresser anyhow sia, your hair damn rabak."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60374265-b52b-4d57-b0f6-1597a31edfbb",
                                                "sense_id": "b4fe65b5-8313-3cdb-b4b8-853a0ebd9049",
                                                "text": "Even the newspaper recommendation oso anyhow one."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ae7f4cb6-750f-47f6-9b7d-56e5bfddb891",
                        "source_entry_id": "700b7626-94ba-36cb-820b-25b2613378fc",
                        "source_sense_id": "5af9adae-5a12-3bad-b771-2acfc5fcfb99",
                        "source_sense_description": "drückt aus, dass etwas auf jeden Fall und unabhängig von allem eintritt",
                        "target_lang_word": "de toute façon",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "de toute façon",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21e6a8af-e5ec-3b6b-97f7-c1553e7b5cdd",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4e7868-2717-316c-947f-2ca46e2d4d27",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "De quelque façon que cela soit ; dans tous les cas ; quelle que soit la situation ; utilisé pour passer outre ou qualifier la notion précédente, ou pour indiquer qu'une affirmation est vraie peu importe l'existence de la notion précédente."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa4815fb-ed2b-4029-b81f-3ccc82fdd37c",
                                                "sense_id": "21e6a8af-e5ec-3b6b-97f7-c1553e7b5cdd",
                                                "text": "4 avril 1871. Ils n'ont encore rien compris. De toute façon les vaincus, ça n'a pas besoin de comprendre. Ça doit accepter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd1e0f56-de1b-4101-beef-5588f54ecbd9",
                                                "sense_id": "21e6a8af-e5ec-3b6b-97f7-c1553e7b5cdd",
                                                "text": "Le téléphone avait sonné plusieurs fois, des cons qu'elle n’avait pu s’empêcher d’envoyer aux pelotes, quelle importance puisque de toute façon, sans le moineau, l’émission était foutue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "626d3a64-c458-4ba5-a474-45ec3de30524",
                                                "sense_id": "21e6a8af-e5ec-3b6b-97f7-c1553e7b5cdd",
                                                "text": "J'aimerais que vous sacrifiiez un haut-parleur, et donc les quelques euros qu'il vous aura coûté. De toute façon, ce sacrifice ne sera pas inutile, car pour comprendre comment fonctionne un composant, rien de mieux que de le démonter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43347be7-2d95-4465-9d21-77da487a8959",
                                                "sense_id": "21e6a8af-e5ec-3b6b-97f7-c1553e7b5cdd",
                                                "text": "— Moi non plus, je n'ai plus de cigarettes, dit-il.\n— Putain de votre race à tous, dit Louise. J'en ai dans mon bungalow au Sun, je vais les chercher. De toute façon, fallait que je m'habille."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
